  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\n`<template for>` can update the DOM declaratively with a certain lifecycle (remove start PI, stream, remove end/marker PI), however there is no way to track it and handle errors or other issues.\n\n\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\nAuthors can use a general purpose mutation observer and \"guess\" that a declarative patch was applied, e.g. by seeing that PIs were removed. This is lossy and costly.\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\nSuggesting to add template information to mutation records.\n\n- A `template` property, a reference to the initiating detached `<template>` element. This can be used to include additional author-provided metadata attributes on the template element and examine them with JS\n- A `templatePhase` property (bikesheddable), which is start/update/end or some such, for the patching phase.\n- Guarantee that each phase patching is an individual mutation record\n\n### Anything else?\n\nSee https://github.com/WICG/declarative-partial-updates/issues/110 for original request for this from OpenAI.",
